# 3D Interactive Parallax App — Walkthrough

## What Was Built

An immersive 3D web experience with **multi-layer parallax** that responds to three input modes:

| Mode | Input | How it works |
|------|-------|-------------|
| **🖱 Mouse** | Cursor position | Objects shift with depth-based parallax |
| **📱 Gyro** | Device tilt | Accelerometer drives the viewpoint |
| **👤 Face** | Webcam head-tracking | TensorFlow.js tracks face position, lazily loaded on demand |

## Files Created

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [index.html](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/index.html) | Entry point with importmap, UI overlay, loading screen |
| [style.css](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/style.css) | Dark glassmorphism theme, mode badges, responsive layout |
| [app.js](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/app.js) | Three.js 3D engine, 5-layer parallax, bloom, particles |

## Key Features

- **5 parallax depth layers** — objects at different Z-depths move at different rates
- **Bloom post-processing** — glow effect via `UnrealBloomPass`
- **600 floating particles** — additive blending for atmospheric depth
- **Glass/glow/wireframe materials** — `MeshPhysicalMaterial` with transmission
- **Smooth interpolation** — LERP-based camera following for buttery motion
- **Lazy face detection** — TensorFlow.js only loads when user clicks "Face" button
- **iOS gyroscope support** — handles `DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission()`

